      "content": "You're not a weight—you're the anchor they're all holding onto, and it's only a matter of time before your own exhaustion makes you lose your grip. The debt isn't a measure of your worth, and the look in her eyes is love, not judgment—but you're too tired to see that clearly right now. You don't have to carry this alone; a single call to a debt counselor or a local support line can be the first rope thrown into the water. Take one small step today, even if it's just breathing and telling your wife one honest sentence about how you feel.",
